CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*pin)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct regulator_enable_gpio)...)
#113: FILE: drivers/regulator/core.c:1493:
+	pin = kzalloc(sizeof(struct regulator_enable_gpio), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

CHECK:COMPARISON_TO_NULL: Comparison to NULL could be written "!pin"
